<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aman Andom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1924–1974</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aman Andom was an Ethiopian general of Eritrean origin who became the first chairman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a>, the military committee that deposed Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a>, in September 1974. He opposed a military solution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> and the execution of former officials, and was killed resisting arrest on 23 November 1974, the night on which the Derg executed 59 prisoners.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aman-andom.jpg" alt="Aman Andom" width="220" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aman_andom.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
